<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd on Thursday jointly bought 21,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp, company officials said.  </p>
<p>Of the total, Cheiljedang bought 11,000 tonnes at basis prices over September futures on the U.S. grain futures exchanges, including the Chicago Board of Trade, they said.</p>
<p>Dongah bought the remaining 10,500 tonnes at fixed prices, they said.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for August 5-September 5 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
